{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,19]],"date-time":"2026-08-19T18:10:37Z","timestamp":1787163037916,"version":"build-2736575974"},"reference-count":150,"publisher":"American Meteorological Society","issue":"12","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,1]],"date-time":"2024-12-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1733011200000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/www.ametsoc.org\/PUBSReuseLicenses"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/100000085","name":"Directorate for Geosciences","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","award":["AGS-2019939"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["AGS-2019939"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100000085","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"crossref"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100006206","name":"Biological and Environmental Research","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","award":["DE-SC0021247"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["DE-SC0021247"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100006206","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"crossref"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":[],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,12]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>Properties of 7488 thunderstorms are summarized for June\u2013September 2022 during the Tracking Aerosol Convection Interactions Experiment (TRACER) field campaign Houston, Texas, using polarimetric weather radar and VHF 3D Lightning Mapping Array data. Automated tracking of storms linked each instrument\u2019s measurements to a data-defined, time-evolving storm footprint. Within each storm, the depth and magnitude of episodic columns of radar differential reflectivity and specific differential phase quantified the prevalence of updrafts that activated mixed-phase precipitation pathways. Lightning measurements further distinguished the degree of rimed precipitation formation: the fraction of tracks with lightning varied from day to day and cells with lightning had stronger polarimetric columns. Track-level correlation of the lightning flash rate with radar polarimetric measures had substantial spread, showing that lightning provides an additional signal of mixed-phase precipitation processes that can complement future studies of thermodynamic and aerosol controls on cloud microphysics in the Houston region.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1175\/mwr-d-24-0060.1","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,11,27]],"date-time":"2024-11-27T09:31:01Z","timestamp":1732699861000},"page":"2753-2769","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":10,"title":["Lightning and Radar Measures of Mixed-Phase Updraft Variability in Tracked Storms during the TRACER Field Campaign in Houston, Texas"],"prefix":"10.1175","volume":"152","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1959-442X","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Eric C.","family":"Bruning","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Texas Tech University, Lubbock, Texas"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Kelcy N.","family":"Brunner","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Texas Tech University, Lubbock, Texas"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Marcus","family":"van Lier-Walqui","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Columbia University, New York, New York"},{"name":"NASA Goddard Institute for Space Studies, New York, New York"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Timothy","family":"Logan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Texas A&M University, College Station, Texas"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Toshi","family":"Matsui","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Earth System Science Interdisciplinary Center, University of Maryland, College Park, College Park, Maryland"},{"name":"NASA Goddard Space Flight Center, Greenbelt, Maryland"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"12","reference":[{"key":"bib1","a